/T (The story of the Exodus is a powerful narrative of liberation and spiritual renewal that begins with the central figure of Moses. Born during a time of oppression for the Hebrews in Egypt, Moses was chosen by God to lead his people to freedom. After a series of miraculous events and confrontations with Pharaoh, including the ten plagues, Moses led the Israelites through the Red Sea, an emblematic moment of liberation symbolizing the breaking of the chains of slavery.)
