/T (The Gospels are central texts for understanding the life and teachings of Jesus Christ. They offer a detailed account of his time on Earth, highlighting his miracles, teachings, and the lasting impact of his message. Miracles and Teachings: The miracles performed by Jesus are described in the Gospels as manifestations of divine power, demonstrating compassion and revealing the nature of the Kingdom of God. Among the most notable are the multiplication of the loaves and fishes, the healing of the sick, and the resurrection of Lazarus. These events not only amazed those present but also served as living parables about faith, hope, and unconditional love. Jesus' teachings, often conveyed through parables, invite followers to a life of humility, justice, and love for one's neighbor. Discourses such as the Sermon on the Mount stand out, where Jesus shares ethical and spiritual principles that continue to inspire millions around the world.)
