/T (The Holy Spirit and the Mission: The book of Acts stands out as a vibrant and inspiring account of the birth and expansion of the Early Church. One of the central themes is the transformative role of the Holy Spirit. On the day of Pentecost, the apostles received the Holy Spirit, which gave them courage and wisdom to proclaim the message of Jesus Christ. This event not only marked the beginning of the apostolic mission but also highlighted how essential the presence of the Holy Spirit was for the spread of the Gospel. Through signs, miracles, and the courage of the apostles, the Holy Spirit guided the young church, strengthening it in times of persecution and uncertainty.)
/E (The Holy Spirit and the Mission: The book of Acts stands out as a vibrant and inspiring account of the birth and expansion of the Early Church. One of the central themes is the transformative role of the Holy Spirit. On the day of Pentecost, the apostles received the Holy Spirit, which gave them courage and wisdom to proclaim the message of Jesus Christ. This event not only marked the beginning of the apostolic mission but also highlighted how essential the presence of the Holy Spirit was for the spread of the Gospel. Through signs, miracles, and the courage of the apostles, the Holy Spirit guided the young church, strengthening it in times of persecution and uncertainty.)
